@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- ca-interpretation-rules.l4
--
-- The Interpretation Act (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. I-21: the other rules that compute.
-- Sections that are only rules of reading (the singular includes the plural, the law is always speaking, and so on) are not forced
-- into code; NOTES.md lists each with its reason.
-- Where a rule has a condition the text states and the caller knows, the condition is an input; where the text names the cases it
-- governs and the caller asks about another, the answer is a named refusal, never FALSE.

§ `Section 3(1), section 8(1) and section 9: application`

-- "Every provision of this Act applies, unless a contrary intention appears, to every enactment, whether enacted before or after the
-- commencement of this Act."
-- src:29 | 3 (1) Every provision of this Act applies, unless a contrary intention appears, to every enactment, whether enacted before or after the commencement of this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act s 3(1) (src:29)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision of the Act applies to an enactment unless` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    NOT `a contrary intention appears`

-- "Every enactment applies to the whole of Canada, unless a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment."
-- src:70 | 8 (1) Every enactment applies to the whole of Canada, unless a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 8(1) (src:70)
GIVEN `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an enactment applies to the whole of Canada unless` `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment` MEANS
    NOT `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment`

-- (2): where an enactment that does not apply to the whole of Canada is amended, no provision in the amending enactment applies to
-- any part of Canada to which the amended enactment does not apply, unless it is provided in the amending enactment that it applies
-- to that part of Canada or to the whole of Canada.
-- Where the amended enactment DOES apply to the part, subsection (2) says nothing and subsection (1) governs.
-- src:72 | (2) Where an enactment that does not apply to the whole of Canada is amended, no provision in the amending enactment applies to any part of Canada to which the amended enactment does not apply, unless it is provided in the amending enactment that it applies to that part of Canada or to the whole of Canada.
-- src:70 | 8 (1) Every enactment applies to the whole of Canada, unless a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 8(2) (src:72) and s 8(1) (src:70)
GIVEN `the amended enactment applies to that part of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amending enactment provides that it applies to that part of Canada or to the whole of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amending enactment expresses a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision of an amending enactment applies to a part of Canada where` `the amended enactment applies to that part of Canada` `and` `the amending enactment provides that it applies to that part of Canada or to the whole of Canada` `and` `the amending enactment expresses a contrary intention` MEANS
    IF   `the amended enactment applies to that part of Canada`
    THEN NOT `the amending enactment expresses a contrary intention`
    ELSE `the amending enactment provides that it applies to that part of Canada or to the whole of Canada`

-- (2.1): an enactment that applies in respect of exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing natural resources, living or
-- non-living, applies in addition to the exclusive economic zone of Canada, unless a contrary intention is expressed.
-- src:74 | (2.1) Every enactment that applies in respect of exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing natural resources, whether living or non-living, applies, in addition to its application to Canada, to the exclusive economic zone of Canada, unless a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 8(2.1) (src:74)
GIVEN `it applies in respect of exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing natural resources, living or non-living` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an enactment applies also to the exclusive economic zone of Canada where` `it applies in respect of exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing natural resources, living or non-living` `and` `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment` MEANS
    IF   `it applies in respect of exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing natural resources, living or non-living`
    THEN NOT `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment`
    ELSE `section 8(2.1) speaks of enactments about natural resources and does not say whether another enactment applies to the exclusive economic zone`

-- src:74 | (2.1) Every enactment that applies in respect of exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing natural resources, whether living or non-living, applies, in addition to its application to Canada, to the exclusive economic zone of Canada, unless a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 8(2.1) (src:74): an enactment not about natural resources is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 8(2.1) speaks of enactments about natural resources and does not say whether another enactment applies to the exclusive economic zone` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 8(2.1) speaks of enactments about natural resources and does not say whether another enactment applies to the exclusive economic zone"

-- (2.2): an enactment that applies in respect of exploring or exploiting (a) mineral or other non-living resources of the seabed or
-- subsoil, or (b) living organisms belonging to sedentary species, applies in addition to the continental shelf of Canada.
-- src:76 | (2.2) Every enactment that applies in respect of exploring or exploiting natural resources that are
-- src:77 | (a) mineral or other non-living resources of the seabed or subsoil, or
-- src:78 | (b) living organisms belonging to sedentary species, that is to say, organisms that, at the harvestable stage, either are immobile on or under the seabed or are unable to move except in constant physical contact with the seabed or subsoil
-- src:79 | applies, in addition to its application to Canada, to the continental shelf of Canada, unless a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 8(2.2) (src:76-79)
GIVEN `it applies in respect of exploring or exploiting mineral or other non-living resources of the seabed or subsoil, or living organisms belonging to sedentary species` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an enactment applies also to the continental shelf of Canada where` `it applies in respect of exploring or exploiting mineral or other non-living resources of the seabed or subsoil, or living organisms belonging to sedentary species` `and` `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment` MEANS
    IF   `it applies in respect of exploring or exploiting mineral or other non-living resources of the seabed or subsoil, or living organisms belonging to sedentary species`
    THEN NOT `a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment`
    ELSE `section 8(2.2) speaks of enactments about seabed and sedentary-species resources and does not say whether another enactment applies to the continental shelf`

