-- src:78 | (b) living organisms belonging to sedentary species, that is to say, organisms that, at the harvestable stage, either are immobile on or under the seabed or are unable to move except in constant physical contact with the seabed or subsoil
-- src:79 | applies, in addition to its application to Canada, to the continental shelf of Canada, unless a contrary intention is expressed in the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 8(2.2) (src:76-79): an enactment not about those resources is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 8(2.2) speaks of enactments about seabed and sedentary-species resources and does not say whether another enactment applies to the continental shelf` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 8(2.2) speaks of enactments about seabed and sedentary-species resources and does not say whether another enactment applies to the continental shelf"

-- 8.2: civil law terminology or meaning in the Province of Quebec, common law elsewhere, "unless otherwise provided by law".
DECLARE `The tradition whose terminology or meaning is adopted` IS ONE OF
    `the civil law terminology or meaning`
    `the common law terminology or meaning`

-- src:89 | 8.2 Unless otherwise provided by law, when an enactment contains both civil law and common law terminology, or terminology that has a different meaning in the civil law and the common law, the civil law terminology or meaning is to be adopted in the Province of Quebec and the common law terminology or meaning is to be adopted in the other provinces.
@ref Interpretation Act s 8.2 (src:89)
GIVEN `the place is the Province of Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise provided by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The tradition whose terminology or meaning is adopted`
`the terminology or meaning adopted, where an enactment contains both civil law and common law terminology, is` `the place is the Province of Quebec` `unless` `it is otherwise provided by law` MEANS
    IF   `it is otherwise provided by law`
    THEN `another law decides which terminology or meaning is adopted and the Act does not say which`
    ELSE IF   `the place is the Province of Quebec`
         THEN `the civil law terminology or meaning`
         ELSE `the common law terminology or meaning`

-- src:89 | 8.2 Unless otherwise provided by law, when an enactment contains both civil law and common law terminology, or terminology that has a different meaning in the civil law and the common law, the civil law terminology or meaning is to be adopted in the Province of Quebec and the common law terminology or meaning is to be adopted in the other provinces.
@ref Interpretation Act s 8.2 (src:89): the exception is left to other law
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`another law decides which terminology or meaning is adopted and the Act does not say which` MEANS
    REFUSE "another law decides which terminology or meaning is adopted and the Act does not say which"

-- 9: "No provision in a private Act affects the rights of any person, except as therein mentioned or referred to."
-- src:99 | 9 No provision in a private Act affects the rights of any person, except as therein mentioned or referred to.
@ref Interpretation Act s 9 (src:99)
GIVEN `the person's rights are mentioned or referred to in the private Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision in a private Act affects a person's rights if` `the person's rights are mentioned or referred to in the private Act` MEANS
    `the person's rights are mentioned or referred to in the private Act`

-- 17: "No enactment is binding on Her Majesty or affects Her Majesty or Her Majesty's rights or prerogatives in any manner, except as
-- mentioned or referred to in the enactment."
-- src:131 | 17 No enactment is binding on Her Majesty or affects Her Majesty or Her Majesty’s rights or prerogatives in any manner, except as mentioned or referred to in the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 17 (src:131)
GIVEN `the enactment mentions or refers to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an enactment binds or affects Her Majesty or Her Majesty's rights or prerogatives if` `the enactment mentions or refers to Her Majesty` MEANS
    `the enactment mentions or refers to Her Majesty`

§ `Section 11: "shall" and "may"`

DECLARE `A word of command or permission` IS ONE OF
    `shall`
    `may`
    `another expression`

DECLARE `How a word of command or permission is construed` IS ONE OF
    `imperative`
    `permissive`

-- src:107 | 11 The expression “shall” is to be construed as imperative and the expression “may” as permissive.
@ref Interpretation Act s 11 (src:107)
GIVEN w IS A `A word of command or permission`
GIVETH A `How a word of command or permission is construed`
`the construction of the expression` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `shall`              THEN `imperative`
    WHEN `may`                THEN `permissive`
    WHEN `another expression` THEN `section 11 construes the expression shall and the expression may and no other`

-- src:107 | 11 The expression “shall” is to be construed as imperative and the expression “may” as permissive.
@ref Interpretation Act s 11 (src:107): no other expression is named
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 11 construes the expression shall and the expression may and no other` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 11 construes the expression shall and the expression may and no other"

§ `Section 19: administering an oath`

DECLARE `A person who may administer an oath` IS ONE OF
    `a person authorized by the enactment or rule to take the evidence`
    `a judge of any court`
    `a notary public`
    `a justice of the peace`
    `a commissioner for taking affidavits`
    `any other person`

-- (1): the oath may be administered, and a certificate given, by (a) any person authorized by the enactment or rule to take the
-- evidence; or (b) a judge, notary public, justice of the peace or commissioner for taking affidavits, having authority or
-- jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered.
-- src:144 | 19 (1) Where, by an enactment or by a rule of the Senate or House of Commons, evidence under oath is authorized or required to be taken, or an oath is authorized or directed to be made, taken or administered, the oath may be administered, and a certificate of its having been made, taken or administered may be given by
-- src:145 | (a) any person authorized by the enactment or rule to take the evidence; or
-- src:146 | (b) a judge of any court, a notary public, a justice of the peace or a commissioner for taking affidavits, having authority or jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered.
@ref Interpretation Act s 19(1) (src:144-146)
GIVEN p IS A `A person who may administer an oath`
      `the person has authority or jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an oath under an enactment or a rule of the Senate or House of Commons may be administered by` p `where` `the person has authority or jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a person authorized by the enactment or rule to take the evidence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a judge of any court`                THEN `the person has authority or jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered`
    WHEN `a notary public`                     THEN `the person has authority or jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered`
    WHEN `a justice of the peace`              THEN `the person has authority or jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered`
    WHEN `a commissioner for taking affidavits` THEN `the person has authority or jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered`
    WHEN `any other person`                    THEN `section 19(1) names who may administer an oath and does not say that anyone else may not`

-- src:144 | 19 (1) Where, by an enactment or by a rule of the Senate or House of Commons, evidence under oath is authorized or required to be taken, or an oath is authorized or directed to be made, taken or administered, the oath may be administered, and a certificate of its having been made, taken or administered may be given by
-- src:145 | (a) any person authorized by the enactment or rule to take the evidence; or
-- src:146 | (b) a judge of any court, a notary public, a justice of the peace or a commissioner for taking affidavits, having authority or jurisdiction within the place where the oath is administered.
@ref Interpretation Act s 19(1) (src:144-146): the list is not said to be exhaustive
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 19(1) names who may administer an oath and does not say that anyone else may not` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 19(1) names who may administer an oath and does not say that anyone else may not"

-- (2): where power is conferred on a justice of the peace to administer an oath or solemn affirmation or to take an affidavit or
-- declaration, the power may be exercised by a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths.
-- src:148 | (2) Where power is conferred on a justice of the peace to administer an oath or solemn affirmation or to take an affidavit or declaration, the power may be exercised by a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths.
@ref Interpretation Act s 19(2) (src:148)
GIVEN `the person is a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a power conferred on a justice of the peace to administer an oath or solemn affirmation or to take an affidavit or declaration may be exercised by a person who is a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths if` `the person is a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths` MEANS
    IF   `the person is a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 19(2) names a notary public and a commissioner for taking oaths and does not say that no one else may exercise the power`

-- src:148 | (2) Where power is conferred on a justice of the peace to administer an oath or solemn affirmation or to take an affidavit or declaration, the power may be exercised by a notary public or a commissioner for taking oaths.
@ref Interpretation Act s 19(2) (src:148): the list is not said to be exhaustive
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 19(2) names a notary public and a commissioner for taking oaths and does not say that no one else may exercise the power` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 19(2) names a notary public and a commissioner for taking oaths and does not say that no one else may exercise the power"

§ `Section 20: a report laid before Parliament at a session`

-- "nothing in the Act shall be construed as requiring the same report or document to be laid before Parliament at any subsequent
-- session", where, in compliance with the Act, it has been laid before Parliament at a session.
-- src:152 | 20 Where an Act requires a report or other document to be laid before Parliament and, in compliance with the Act, a particular report or document has been laid before Parliament at a session thereof, nothing in the Act shall be construed as requiring the same report or document to be laid before Parliament at any subsequent session.
@ref Interpretation Act s 20 (src:152)
GIVEN `it has been laid before Parliament at a session in compliance with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Act that requires a report or document to be laid before Parliament requires it to be laid again at a subsequent session if` `it has been laid before Parliament at a session in compliance with the Act` MEANS
    IF   `it has been laid before Parliament at a session in compliance with the Act`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `section 20 speaks of a report or document already laid at a session and does not say whether one not yet laid is required again`

-- src:152 | 20 Where an Act requires a report or other document to be laid before Parliament and, in compliance with the Act, a particular report or document has been laid before Parliament at a session thereof, nothing in the Act shall be construed as requiring the same report or document to be laid before Parliament at any subsequent session.
@ref Interpretation Act s 20 (src:152): a report not yet laid is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 20 speaks of a report or document already laid at a session and does not say whether one not yet laid is required again` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 20 speaks of a report or document already laid at a session and does not say whether one not yet laid is required again"

§ `Section 21: corporations`

DECLARE `A power or immunity` IS ONE OF
    `the power to sue and be sued`
    `the power to contract and be contracted with by its corporate name`
    `the power to have a common seal and to alter or change it at pleasure`
    `the power to have perpetual succession`
    `the power to acquire and hold personal property for the purposes for which the corporation is established and to alienate that property at pleasure`
    `the power to use either the English or the French form of its name or both forms, and to show both forms on its seal or have two seals`
    `the power of a majority of the members to bind the others by their acts`
    `exemption of individual members who do not contravene the provisions of the enactment from personal liability for its debts, obligations or acts`
    `the power to carry on the business of banking`

-- (1): words establishing a corporation shall be construed as vesting (a) the six powers of paragraph (a); (b) in a corporation whose
-- name consists of an English and a French form or a combined form, the power over the forms of its name and seal; (c) in a majority
-- of the members the power to bind the others; and (d) as exempting from personal liability individual members who do not contravene the
-- provisions of the enactment.  (3): no corporation is deemed authorized to carry on banking unless the power is expressly conferred.
-- src:156 | 21 (1) Words establishing a corporation shall be construed
-- src:157 | (a) as vesting in the corporation power to sue and be sued, to contract and be contracted with by its corporate name, to have a common seal and to alter or change it at pleasure, to have perpetual succession, to acquire and hold personal property for the purposes for which the corporation is established and to alienate that property at pleasure;
-- src:158 | (b) in the case of a corporation having a name consisting of an English and a French form or a combined English and French form, as vesting in the corporation power to use either the English or the French form of its name or both forms and to show on its seal both the English and French forms of its name or have two seals, one showing the English and the other showing the French form of its name;
-- src:159 | (c) as vesting in a majority of the members of the corporation the power to bind the others by their acts; and
-- src:160 | (d) as exempting from personal liability for its debts, obligations or acts individual members of the corporation who do not contravene the provisions of the enactment establishing the corporation.
-- src:164 | (3) No corporation is deemed to be authorized to carry on the business of banking unless that power is expressly conferred on it by the enactment establishing the corporation.
@ref Interpretation Act s 21(1) (src:156-160) and s 21(3) (src:164)
GIVEN x IS A `A power or immunity`
      `its name consists of an English and a French form or a combined English and French form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member contravenes the provisions of the enactment establishing the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power to carry on the business of banking is expressly conferred by the enactment establishing the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words establishing a corporation vest it with` x `where` `its name consists of an English and a French form or a combined English and French form` `and` `a member contravenes the provisions of the enactment establishing the corporation` `and` `the power to carry on the business of banking is expressly conferred by the enactment establishing the corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `the power to sue and be sued` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the power to contract and be contracted with by its corporate name` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the power to have a common seal and to alter or change it at pleasure` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the power to have perpetual succession` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the power to acquire and hold personal property for the purposes for which the corporation is established and to alienate that property at pleasure` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the power to use either the English or the French form of its name or both forms, and to show both forms on its seal or have two seals` THEN
        IF   `its name consists of an English and a French form or a combined English and French form`
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE `section 21(1)(b) vests the power in a corporation whose name has an English and a French form and does not say that any other corporation lacks it`
    WHEN `the power of a majority of the members to bind the others by their acts` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `exemption of individual members who do not contravene the provisions of the enactment from personal liability for its debts, obligations or acts` THEN
        IF   `a member contravenes the provisions of the enactment establishing the corporation`
        THEN `section 21(1)(d) exempts members who do not contravene and does not say whether one who does contravene is exempt`
        ELSE TRUE
    WHEN `the power to carry on the business of banking` THEN
        `the power to carry on the business of banking is expressly conferred by the enactment establishing the corporation`

-- src:158 | (b) in the case of a corporation having a name consisting of an English and a French form or a combined English and French form, as vesting in the corporation power to use either the English or the French form of its name or both forms and to show on its seal both the English and French forms of its name or have two seals, one showing the English and the other showing the French form of its name;
@ref Interpretation Act s 21(1)(b) (src:158): no negative rule
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 21(1)(b) vests the power in a corporation whose name has an English and a French form and does not say that any other corporation lacks it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 21(1)(b) vests the power in a corporation whose name has an English and a French form and does not say that any other corporation lacks it"

-- src:160 | (d) as exempting from personal liability for its debts, obligations or acts individual members of the corporation who do not contravene the provisions of the enactment establishing the corporation.
@ref Interpretation Act s 21(1)(d) (src:160): a contravening member is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 21(1)(d) exempts members who do not contravene and does not say whether one who does contravene is exempt` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 21(1)(d) exempts members who do not contravene and does not say whether one who does contravene is exempt"

§ `Section 22: majorities and quorum`

-- (1): where an enactment requires or authorizes more than two persons to do an act or thing, a majority of them may do it.
-- A majority is more than half.
-- src:168 | 22 (1) Where an enactment requires or authorizes more than two persons to do an act or thing, a majority of them may do it.
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(1) (src:168)
GIVEN `the number of persons the enactment requires or authorizes to do it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smallest number that is a majority of the persons an enactment requires or authorizes to do a thing, when they number` `the number of persons the enactment requires or authorizes to do it` MEANS
    IF       `the number of persons the enactment requires or authorizes to do it` GREATER THAN 2
         AND FLOOR `the number of persons the enactment requires or authorizes to do it` EQUALS `the number of persons the enactment requires or authorizes to do it`
    THEN (FLOOR (`the number of persons the enactment requires or authorizes to do it` DIVIDED BY 2)) PLUS 1
    ELSE `section 22(1) speaks of more than two persons and says nothing of one or two`

-- src:168 | 22 (1) Where an enactment requires or authorizes more than two persons to do an act or thing, a majority of them may do it.
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(1) (src:168): two persons or fewer are not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 22(1) speaks of more than two persons and says nothing of one or two` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 22(1) speaks of more than two persons and says nothing of one or two"

-- (2)(a): a number of members equal to (i) if the number of members is a fixed number, at least one-half of the number of members,
-- constitutes a quorum.
-- src:171 | (a) at a meeting of the association, a number of members of the association equal to,
-- src:172 | (i) if the number of members provided for by the enactment is a fixed number, at least one-half of the number of members, and
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(2)(a)(i) (src:171-172)
GIVEN `the number of members provided for by the enactment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a quorum exists, where the number of members is fixed at` `the number of members provided for by the enactment` `and the number present is` `the number of members present` MEANS
    IF   `the number of members provided for by the enactment` AT LEAST 3
    THEN `the number of members present` AT LEAST (`the number of members provided for by the enactment` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE `section 22(2) speaks of an association of three or more members and says nothing of fewer`

-- (ii): if the number provided for is not a fixed number but is within a range having a maximum or minimum, at least one-half of the
-- number of members in office if that number is within the range.
-- src:173 | (ii) if the number of members provided for by the enactment is not a fixed number but is within a range having a maximum or minimum, at least one-half of the number of members in office if that number is within the range,
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(2)(a)(ii) (src:173)
GIVEN `the number of members in office` IS A NUMBER
      `the least number the range allows` IS A NUMBER
      `the greatest number the range allows` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a quorum exists, where the members in office number` `the number of members in office` `and the range runs from` `the least number the range allows` `to` `the greatest number the range allows` `and the number present is` `the number of members present` MEANS
    IF       `the number of members in office` AT LEAST `the least number the range allows`
         AND `the number of members in office` AT MOST `the greatest number the range allows`
    THEN `the number of members present` AT LEAST (`the number of members in office` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE `section 22(2)(a)(ii) speaks of a number of members in office that is within the range and says nothing of one that is not`

-- src:170 | (2) Where an enactment establishes a board, court, commission or other body consisting of three or more members, in this section called an “association”,
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(2) (src:170): fewer than three members are not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 22(2) speaks of an association of three or more members and says nothing of fewer` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 22(2) speaks of an association of three or more members and says nothing of fewer"

-- src:173 | (ii) if the number of members provided for by the enactment is not a fixed number but is within a range having a maximum or minimum, at least one-half of the number of members in office if that number is within the range,
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(2)(a)(ii) (src:173): a number outside the range is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 22(2)(a)(ii) speaks of a number of members in office that is within the range and says nothing of one that is not` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 22(2)(a)(ii) speaks of a number of members in office that is within the range and says nothing of one that is not"

-- (b): an act or thing done by a majority of the members of the association present at a meeting, if the members present constitute a
-- quorum, is deemed to have been done by the association.
-- src:175 | (b) an act or thing done by a majority of the members of the association present at a meeting, if the members present constitute a quorum, is deemed to have been done by the association; and
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(2)(b) (src:175)
GIVEN `the number of them who did it` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER
      `the members present constitute a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an act or thing done at a meeting by` `the number of them who did it` `of` `the number of members present` `members present is deemed done by the association where` `the members present constitute a quorum` MEANS
    IF   `the members present constitute a quorum`
    THEN `the number of them who did it` GREATER THAN (`the number of members present` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE `section 22(2)(b) deems an act done by the association only where the members present constitute a quorum and says nothing of one done otherwise`

-- src:175 | (b) an act or thing done by a majority of the members of the association present at a meeting, if the members present constitute a quorum, is deemed to have been done by the association; and
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(2)(b) (src:175): a meeting without a quorum is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 22(2)(b) deems an act done by the association only where the members present constitute a quorum and says nothing of one done otherwise` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 22(2)(b) deems an act done by the association only where the members present constitute a quorum and says nothing of one done otherwise"

-- (c): a vacancy in the membership does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right of the members in
-- office to act, if the number in office is not less than a quorum.
-- src:176 | (c) a vacancy in the membership of the association does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right of the members in office to act, if the number of members in office is not less than a quorum.
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(2)(c) (src:176)
GIVEN `the number of members in office` IS A NUMBER
      `the number that constitutes a quorum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a vacancy does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right to act, where` `the number of members in office` `are in office and a quorum is` `the number that constitutes a quorum` MEANS
    IF   `the number of members in office` AT LEAST `the number that constitutes a quorum`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 22(2)(c) protects the association where the members in office are not fewer than a quorum and says nothing of fewer`

-- src:176 | (c) a vacancy in the membership of the association does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right of the members in office to act, if the number of members in office is not less than a quorum.
@ref Interpretation Act s 22(2)(c) (src:176): fewer than a quorum is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 22(2)(c) protects the association where the members in office are not fewer than a quorum and says nothing of fewer` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 22(2)(c) protects the association where the members in office are not fewer than a quorum and says nothing of fewer"

§ `Section 23(1): public officers hold office during pleasure`

-- "Every public officer appointed by or under the authority of an enactment or otherwise is deemed to have been appointed to hold
-- office during pleasure only, unless it is otherwise expressed in the enactment, commission or instrument of appointment."
-- src:180 | 23 (1) Every public officer appointed by or under the authority of an enactment or otherwise is deemed to have been appointed to hold office during pleasure only, unless it is otherwise expressed in the enactment, commission or instrument of appointment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 23(1) (src:180)
GIVEN `it is otherwise expressed in the enactment, commission or instrument of appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a public officer is deemed appointed to hold office during pleasure only unless` `it is otherwise expressed in the enactment, commission or instrument of appointment` MEANS
    NOT `it is otherwise expressed in the enactment, commission or instrument of appointment`

§ `Section 25(1): a document that is evidence of a fact`

DECLARE `What section 25(1) makes of a document` IS ONE OF
    `the document is admissible in evidence and the fact is deemed to be established`
    `the document is admissible in evidence and the fact is not deemed to be established by this subsection, there being evidence to the contrary`

-- src:209 | 25 (1) Where an enactment provides that a document is evidence of a fact without anything in the context to indicate that the document is conclusive evidence, then, in any judicial proceedings, the document is admissible in evidence and the fact is deemed to be established in the absence of any evidence to the contrary.
@ref Interpretation Act s 25(1) (src:209)
GIVEN `something in the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What section 25(1) makes of a document`
`in judicial proceedings, where an enactment provides that a document is evidence of a fact, and` `something in the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence` `and` `there is evidence to the contrary` MEANS
    IF   `something in the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence`
    THEN `section 25(1) applies only where nothing in the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence`
    ELSE IF   `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN `the document is admissible in evidence and the fact is not deemed to be established by this subsection, there being evidence to the contrary`
         ELSE `the document is admissible in evidence and the fact is deemed to be established`

-- src:209 | 25 (1) Where an enactment provides that a document is evidence of a fact without anything in the context to indicate that the document is conclusive evidence, then, in any judicial proceedings, the document is admissible in evidence and the fact is deemed to be established in the absence of any evidence to the contrary.
@ref Interpretation Act s 25(1) (src:209): a document indicated to be conclusive is outside the subsection
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 25(1) applies only where nothing in the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 25(1) applies only where nothing in the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence"

§ `Section 32: forms`

-- "Where a form is prescribed, deviations from that form, not affecting the substance or calculated to mislead, do not invalidate the
-- form used."  A deviation that affects the substance or is calculated to mislead is not said to invalidate it, or not to.
-- src:246 | 32 Where a form is prescribed, deviations from that form, not affecting the substance or calculated to mislead, do not invalidate the form used.
@ref Interpretation Act s 32 (src:246)
GIVEN `the deviation affects the substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deviation is calculated to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a deviation from a prescribed form does not invalidate the form used where` `the deviation affects the substance` `and` `the deviation is calculated to mislead` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `the deviation affects the substance`) AND (NOT `the deviation is calculated to mislead`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 32 saves a deviation that does not affect the substance and is not calculated to mislead and does not say what follows from any other`

-- src:246 | 32 Where a form is prescribed, deviations from that form, not affecting the substance or calculated to mislead, do not invalidate the form used.
@ref Interpretation Act s 32 (src:246): other deviations are not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 32 saves a deviation that does not affect the substance and is not calculated to mislead and does not say what follows from any other` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 32 saves a deviation that does not affect the substance and is not calculated to mislead and does not say what follows from any other"

§ `Section 34: offences`

DECLARE `A class of offence` IS ONE OF
    `an indictable offence`
    `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- (1)(a): the offence is deemed to be an indictable offence if the enactment provides that the offender may be prosecuted for the
-- offence by indictment.  (b): deemed to be one punishable on summary conviction if there is nothing in the context to indicate that
-- the offence is an indictable offence.
-- src:257 | (a) the offence is deemed to be an indictable offence if the enactment provides that the offender may be prosecuted for the offence by indictment;
-- src:258 | (b) the offence is deemed to be one for which the offender is punishable on summary conviction if there is nothing in the context to indicate that the offence is an indictable offence; and
@ref Interpretation Act s 34(1)(a) (src:257) and s 34(1)(b) (src:258)
GIVEN `the enactment provides that the offender may be prosecuted for the offence by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `something in the context indicates that the offence is an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A class of offence`
`the class of an offence created by an enactment where` `the enactment provides that the offender may be prosecuted for the offence by indictment` `and` `something in the context indicates that the offence is an indictable offence` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment provides that the offender may be prosecuted for the offence by indictment`
    THEN `an indictable offence`
    ELSE IF   `something in the context indicates that the offence is an indictable offence`
         THEN `section 34(1) deems an offence indictable only where the enactment provides for prosecution by indictment, and summary only where nothing in the context indicates it indictable`
         ELSE `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:257 | (a) the offence is deemed to be an indictable offence if the enactment provides that the offender may be prosecuted for the offence by indictment;
-- src:258 | (b) the offence is deemed to be one for which the offender is punishable on summary conviction if there is nothing in the context to indicate that the offence is an indictable offence; and
@ref Interpretation Act s 34(1) (src:257-258): an offence indicated indictable by context alone is neither (a) nor (b)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 34(1) deems an offence indictable only where the enactment provides for prosecution by indictment, and summary only where nothing in the context indicates it indictable` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 34(1) deems an offence indictable only where the enactment provides for prosecution by indictment, and summary only where nothing in the context indicates it indictable"

-- (c): if the offence is one for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment or for which the offender is punishable on
-- summary conviction, no person shall be considered to have been convicted of an indictable offence by reason only of having been
-- convicted of the offence on summary conviction.
-- src:259 | (c) if the offence is one for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment or for which the offender is punishable on summary conviction, no person shall be considered to have been convicted of an indictable offence by reason only of having been convicted of the offence on summary conviction.
@ref Interpretation Act s 34(1)(c) (src:259)
GIVEN `the offence is one for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment or is punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person convicted on summary conviction is considered convicted of an indictable offence by reason only of that conviction where` `the offence is one for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment or is punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF   `the offence is one for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment or is punishable on summary conviction`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `section 34(1)(c) speaks of an offence that may be prosecuted by indictment or punished on summary conviction and says nothing of any other`

-- src:259 | (c) if the offence is one for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment or for which the offender is punishable on summary conviction, no person shall be considered to have been convicted of an indictable offence by reason only of having been convicted of the offence on summary conviction.
@ref Interpretation Act s 34(1)(c) (src:259): an offence of one kind only is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 34(1)(c) speaks of an offence that may be prosecuted by indictment or punished on summary conviction and says nothing of any other` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 34(1)(c) speaks of an offence that may be prosecuted by indictment or punished on summary conviction and says nothing of any other"

-- (2): all the provisions of the Criminal Code relating to indictable offences apply to indictable offences created by an enactment,
-- and all those relating to summary conviction offences apply to all other offences created by an enactment, except to the extent
-- that the enactment otherwise provides.
DECLARE `Which provisions of the Criminal Code apply` IS ONE OF
    `the provisions relating to indictable offences`
    `the provisions relating to summary conviction offences`

-- src:261 | (2) All the provisions of the Criminal Code relating to indictable offences apply to indictable offences created by an enactment, and all the provisions of that Code relating to summary conviction offences apply to all other offences created by an enactment, except to the extent that the enactment otherwise provides.
@ref Interpretation Act s 34(2) (src:261)
GIVEN c IS A `A class of offence`
      `the enactment otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Which provisions of the Criminal Code apply`
`the provisions of the Criminal Code that apply to an offence of the class` c `unless` `the enactment otherwise provides` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment otherwise provides`
    THEN `the enactment decides to the extent that it otherwise provides, and the Act does not say what that is`
    ELSE CONSIDER c
         WHEN `an indictable offence` THEN `the provisions relating to indictable offences`
         WHEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN `the provisions relating to summary conviction offences`

-- src:261 | (2) All the provisions of the Criminal Code relating to indictable offences apply to indictable offences created by an enactment, and all the provisions of that Code relating to summary conviction offences apply to all other offences created by an enactment, except to the extent that the enactment otherwise provides.
@ref Interpretation Act s 34(2) (src:261): to the extent the enactment otherwise provides
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the enactment decides to the extent that it otherwise provides, and the Act does not say what that is` MEANS
    REFUSE "the enactment decides to the extent that it otherwise provides, and the Act does not say what that is"

-- (3): in a commission, proclamation, warrant or other document relating to criminal law or procedure in criminal matters,
-- (a) a reference to an offence for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment is a reference to an indictable offence; and
-- (b) a reference to any other offence is a reference to an offence for which the offender is punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:263 | (3) In a commission, proclamation, warrant or other document relating to criminal law or procedure in criminal matters,
-- src:264 | (a) a reference to an offence for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment shall be construed as a reference to an indictable offence; and
-- src:265 | (b) a reference to any other offence shall be construed as a reference to an offence for which the offender is punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Interpretation Act s 34(3) (src:263-265)
GIVEN `the reference is to an offence for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A class of offence`
`the class an offence is construed to be, where a document relating to criminal law or procedure refers to it and` `the reference is to an offence for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment` MEANS
    IF   `the reference is to an offence for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment`
    THEN `an indictable offence`
    ELSE `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 41(1): a reference to two or more provisions by number or letter`

-- "A reference in an enactment by number or letter to two or more parts, divisions, sections ... shall be read as including the number
-- or letter first mentioned and the number or letter last mentioned."  The section says that the two ends are included.
-- A number between them is in the reference by its own words ("from 12 to 16" names 13, 14 and 15), so it is TRUE too.
-- The section does not say whether a number outside the two ends is included, so that refuses.
-- (Pass 1 refused a number between the ends as well; that was an over-refusal, corrected 2026-10-29 and logged in NOTES.md.)
-- The ends are tested on their own, so a reference written the other way round ("from 16 to 12") still includes its two ends.
-- src:391 | 41 (1) A reference in an enactment by number or letter to two or more parts, divisions, sections, subsections, paragraphs, subparagraphs, clauses, subclauses, schedules, appendices or forms shall be read as including the number or letter first mentioned and the number or letter last mentioned.
@ref Interpretation Act s 41(1) (src:391)
GIVEN `the number first mentioned` IS A NUMBER
      `the number last mentioned` IS A NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference from` `the number first mentioned` `to` `the number last mentioned` `includes` n MEANS
    IF       n EQUALS `the number first mentioned`
          OR n EQUALS `the number last mentioned`
          OR (n GREATER THAN `the number first mentioned` AND n LESS THAN `the number last mentioned`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 41(1) says that the two ends and the numbers between them are included and says nothing of a number outside them`

-- src:391 | 41 (1) A reference in an enactment by number or letter to two or more parts, divisions, sections, subsections, paragraphs, subparagraphs, clauses, subclauses, schedules, appendices or forms shall be read as including the number or letter first mentioned and the number or letter last mentioned.
@ref Interpretation Act s 41(1) (src:391): a number outside the two ends is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 41(1) says that the two ends and the numbers between them are included and says nothing of a number outside them` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 41(1) says that the two ends and the numbers between them are included and says nothing of a number outside them"

§ `Section 35(1): "corporation" and "security"`

-- "corporation does not include a partnership that is considered to be a separate legal entity under provincial law".
-- The definition excludes; it does not say what a corporation is, so whether the thing is a corporation otherwise is an input.
-- src:293 | corporation does not include a partnership that is considered to be a separate legal entity under provincial law; (personne morale)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "corporation" (src:293)
GIVEN `it is a corporation apart from this exclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a partnership that is considered to be a separate legal entity under provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`in an enactment, a corporation is` `it is a corporation apart from this exclusion` `and not` `it is a partnership that is considered to be a separate legal entity under provincial law` MEANS
        `it is a corporation apart from this exclusion`
    AND NOT `it is a partnership that is considered to be a separate legal entity under provincial law`

-- "security means sufficient security, and sureties means sufficient sureties, and when those words are used one person is sufficient
-- therefor, unless otherwise expressly required".
-- src:334 | security means sufficient security, and sureties means sufficient sureties, and when those words are used one person is sufficient therefor, unless otherwise expressly required; (caution ou cautionnement)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "security" (src:334)
GIVEN `the number of persons otherwise expressly required` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of persons sufficient for security or sureties, given any number expressly required, which is` `the number of persons otherwise expressly required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of persons otherwise expressly required`
    WHEN JUST n  THEN n
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 1

